.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt CLAUDE-STEPBOARD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm claude-stepboard
.Nd the Claude Code CLI in a browser tab, with a panel of prompt buttons beside it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm start
.Op Fl -dev
.Op Fl y | Fl -yes
.Op Fl -no-input
.Op Fl -no-open
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Op Ar N ...
.Op Fl a | Fl -all
.Op Fl -with-claude
.Nm
.Cm man
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl -help
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
starts a StepBoard session: the real
.Xr claude 1
running in a
.Xr tmux 1
session, a terminal bridge
.Pq Xr ttyd 1
on a private unix socket, a small FastAPI server, and a Safari tab that draws
the terminal on the left and the panel on the right.
.Pp
Every run adds an independent session
.Ar N ,
starting at 1.
When a session is already running,
.Nm
asks
.Sq create session N? [Y/n] ;
Enter means yes.
It only asks when standard input is a terminal: otherwise, or with
.Fl -no-input ,
it exits 1 instead, and
.Fl y
answers yes up front.
.Pp
claude runs as a background session in the Claude daemon
.Pq Li claude --bg ,
one per board slot, named
.Dq StepBoard N .
The board only views it: tmux session
.Li sb Ns Ar N
runs
.Li claude attach Ar id .
Closing the board \(em the tab, the launcher, Ctrl-C,
.Cm stop
or Ctrl-Shift-Q \(em never stops claude.
The next launch of slot
.Ar N ,
or
.Li claude attach Ar id
from any terminal, picks it up where it was, draft included.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm start Oo Fl -dev Oc Oo Fl y Oc Oo Fl -no-input Oc Oo Fl -no-open Oc
The default command.
Starts board
.Ar N
in the next free slot and opens it in Safari.
Serves the built panel
.Pq Pa ui/dist
from the API server on port 8000+N: no Node, no reloader, about 80 MB per
session; rebuilds
.Pa ui/dist
first if anything under
.Pa ui/
is newer than it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -dev
For working on StepBoard itself: Vite serves the panel on port 5172+N with hot
reload, and the API server restarts when
.Pa serve.py
changes.
About 480 MB per session.
.It Fl y , Fl -yes
Don't ask; use the next free slot.
.It Fl -no-input
Never prompt; exit 1 where a question would be asked.
.It Fl -no-open
Don't open Safari.
.El
.It Cm list Op Fl -json
Lists slots: the board
.Pq mode and URL ,
the slot's claude
.Pq id and status in the Claude daemon ,
and leftovers \(em StepBoard API servers still holding port 8000+N with no
board, e.g. from a crash or an older launcher.
.Cm ls
is an alias.
With
.Fl -json ,
prints one JSON array on standard output.
.It Cm stop Oo Ar N ... Oc Oo Fl a Oc Op Fl -with-claude
Closes the given boards: stops their servers, closes their Safari tabs, ends
the tmux viewers
.Li sb Ns Ar N ,
and removes any leftover API server on port 8000+N.
Their claude sessions keep running in the Claude daemon.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl -all
Every slot.
.It Fl -with-claude
Also stop those boards' claude sessions
.Pq Li claude stop Ar id ;
their chats are kept.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Ar N
or
.Fl a ,
it acts only when exactly one board is running.
It only ever touches what the launcher recorded in its run file, the exact
tmux session name, the slot's own claude id, and a
.Li serve:app
process from a StepBoard checkout listening on exactly that slot's port \(em
never a name pattern, never the tmux server, never any other claude session.
.It Cm man
Shows this page.
.It Cm help Op Ar command
Help for
.Ar command ,
or the overview.
Every command also takes
.Fl h
and
.Fl -help .
.It Fl -version
Prints the version and the source revision.
.El
.Pp
Every command also takes
.Fl -no-color .
The older forms
.Cm use ,
.Cm dev
and
.Cm stop all
still work and print their new spelling:
.Cm start ,
.Cm start Fl -dev
and
.Cm stop Fl -all .
A mistyped command gets a
.Dq Did you mean
suggestion.
.Sh SESSIONS
.Bl -column "session" "sbN" "$TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock" "8000+N" "5172+N"
.It Em session Ta Em tmux Ta Em terminal socket Ta Em panel Ta Em dev panel
.It 1 Ta sb1 Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-1.sock Ta 8001 Ta 5173
.It 2 Ta sb2 Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-2.sock Ta 8002 Ta 5174
.It N Ta sbN Ta $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock Ta 8000+N Ta 5172+N
.El
.Sh KEYS
In the panel
.Pq also listed in its SHORTCUTS card :
.Bl -tag -width "Cm Ctrl-Shift-Q"
.It Cm Cmd-J
Jump to the terminal.
.It Cm Cmd-K
Jump to the composer.
.It Cm Cmd-Shift-L
Grab the terminal selection into the composer
.Pq Cm Ctrl-Shift-L No too .
.It Cm Option-1..9
Arm or disarm prompt 1..9.
.It Cm Return
Send, from anywhere outside the terminal.
.It Cm Ctrl-Shift-Q
Close this StepBoard.
It asks first: Return closes the board and keeps claude running,
Option-Return stops claude too, Escape cancels.
.It Cm Shift-Return
New line, in the composer and in the terminal.
.It Cm Up , Cm Down
Walk the history once the caret is at the edge of the composer.
.It Cm Cmd-A
Select all of the draft.
.It Cm drag
Select text in the terminal; it is copied to the clipboard.
.It Cm Escape
In the prompt editor: back out of the delete confirm, then the form, then
edit mode.
.El
.Pp
Lines starting with
.Ql /command
or
.Ql \&!shell
are sent exactly as typed.
Anything else gets the armed prompts and the Length/Format/Edits clauses
appended; the line under the composer shows what.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Set to anything to turn colour off
.Pq also Fl -no-color ;
colour is also off when standard error is not a terminal.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Where the per-slot claude ids live
.Pq default Pa ~/.local/state .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where the run files and sockets live
.Pq default Pa /tmp .
.It Ev SB_SESSION , Ev SB_TTYD_SOCK , Ev SB_PROMPTS
Set by the launcher for
.Pa serve.py ;
set them yourself only to run the server by hand, e.g. for the tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.run
The launcher's PID and its children's PIDs.
.Cm stop
reads it; the launcher removes it on exit.
.It Pa $TMPDIR/stepboard-N.sock
The ttyd socket.
Only local processes can reach it; the page talks to it through
.Pa /api/ws .
.It Pa ~/.local/state/stepboard/claude-N.id
The id of slot
.Ar N Ns 's
background claude
.Po
.Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
moves it
.Pc .
Delete it to give the slot a fresh claude next launch.
.It Pa prompts.json
The prompt buttons, next to
.Pa serve.py ,
shared by every session.
.Ev SB_PROMPTS
moves it.
.It Pa ~/.claude/projects/
Where claude keeps the chat, which is what
.Li /resume
reads.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success, including answering no to
.Sq create session N? .
.It 1
Something failed: a board could not start, a slot to stop was not found, or a
question was needed under
.Fl -no-input .
.It 2
Usage error: unknown command or option, a bad session number, or an ambiguous
bare
.Cm stop .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the default board and open it in Safari:
.Dl claude-stepboard
.Pp
Hack on the panel with hot reload, in a second slot, without being asked:
.Dl claude-stepboard start --dev --yes
.Pp
Restart board 2 to pick up new code; its claude keeps running:
.Dl claude-stepboard stop 2 && claude-stepboard
.Pp
See what is running, or feed it to a script:
.Dl claude-stepboard list
.Dl claude-stepboard list --json | jq '.[].claude'
.Pp
Close every board and stop their claudes:
.Dl claude-stepboard stop --all --with-claude
.Pp
Open board 2's claude in a plain terminal, without the board:
.Dl claude attach $(cat ~/.local/state/stepboard/claude-2.id)
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr claude 1 ,
.Xr tmux 1 ,
.Xr ttyd 1
.Pp
.Pa README.md
and
.Pa SUMMARY.md
in the repository.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
A web terminal is a full shell.
ttyd has no TCP port.
The API refuses any Host other than localhost or 127.0.0.1 and any
cross-site Origin, which blocks DNS rebinding and cross-site WebSocket
hijacking.
